    <h2 id="defensive-heading">Defensive publication track</h2>
    <p>
      Patent <strong>E</strong> is the one accessibility-portfolio
      idea that ships as <strong>defensive publication</strong> rather
      than as a provisional filing. The Patent E methodology is
      drafted as an arXiv preprint &mdash; with full algorithmic
      disclosure and benchmarks &mdash; and deposited before any
      commercial release. The defensive-publication route establishes
      the date of disclosure as prior art against future third-party
      filings on the same technique, without committing the portfolio
      to a multi-year prosecution cost on a low-monetisation idea.
    </p>
    <p>
      Patent F (predictive backlog optimisation) follows a hybrid
      defensive posture: the provisional is filed (claim coverage
      preserved) <em>and</em> the methodology paper is deposited on
      arXiv (defensive disclosure broadens the prior-art record without
      narrowing the filed scope). Patent G methodology is also
      scheduled for an arXiv methodology paper in Wave 2 as part of
      the HYBRID OSS-plus-defensive-publication pattern.
    </p>
  </section>

